From 1008fa4941f13d941357c7c84c31aec6fe083c27 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Harvester57 <1315-Harvester57@users.noreply.git.frama-c.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 23:56:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [libc] syslog.h: include __fc_string_axiomatic.h for Variadic

The Variadic translation classifies syslog() as a printf-like function and generates valid_read_string / valid_read_nstring preconditions on its format string and string arguments. Because share/libc/syslog.h did not include __fc_string_axiomatic.h, a file including only <syslog.h> triggered a kernel:libc:frama-c warning and lost all string-validity preconditions on syslog() calls.

Include __fc_string_axiomatic.h in share/libc/syslog.h (matching stdio.h, pwd.h, unistd.h, fcntl.h, wchar.h, and other POSIX headers).

New test: tests/libc/syslog_h.c.
---
 share/libc/syslog.h                     |  1 +
 tests/libc/oracle/syslog_h.0.res.oracle | 41 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 tests/libc/syslog_h.c                   | 22 +++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 64 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/libc/oracle/syslog_h.0.res.oracle
 create mode 100644 tests/libc/syslog_h.c

diff --git a/share/libc/syslog.h b/share/libc/syslog.h
index 54191cb99f..cc86ca4474 100644
--- a/share/libc/syslog.h
+++ b/share/libc/syslog.h
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include "features.h"
 __PUSH_FC_STDLIB
 #include "__fc_define_null.h"
+#include "__fc_string_axiomatic.h"
 #include <stdarg.h>
 
 __BEGIN_DECLS
